                <pb facs="0841" n="829" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg829"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867.00/3132: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Steinhardt</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-04-01T00:00:00-04:00">April 1,
                            1942—midnight</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>118. Your 234, March 31, 2 p.m. In reply to a telegraphic inquiry from Thurston,
                    the Department sent him the following telegram on March 25:</p>
                <p>[Here follows text of telegram No. 139, March 25, 9 p.m., to the Chargé in the
                    Soviet Union, printed on <ref target="#pg827">page 827</ref>.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
